  bootwright / machine disk-check
      Compare the specified disk identity with whole devices visible to this Linux boot. The
      report shows redacted identity comparisons, exact capacity and stability. Run on the
      target machine from the RHCOS live shell for installation rehearsal.

  Usage
    bootwright machine disk-check [flags]

  Command flags
      --serial-number  Expected exact disk serial number
      --size-bytes     Expected exact capacity in bytes (required)
      --wwn            Expected disk WWN as a nonzero 0x-prefixed NAA identity (required)

  Common flags
      --ascii       Use ASCII status markers
      --color       Select terminal colors (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --detail      Select human detail (values: compact, full) · default compact
      -h, --help    Show help for this command
      -o, --output  Select output mode (values: text, json, yaml) · default text
      --progress    Select progress animation (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --width       Set presentation width (0: automatic) · default 0

  Examples
    bootwright machine disk-check --wwn 0x5000000000000001 --size-bytes 8192
